; bearing-chain-band.fk — the reachable spatial chain, and the link that is unmeasured.
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk observe/bearing-chain.fk
;
; Grounded 2026-07-23 on R5CW20DK17A: stereo mic pair ~160 mm apart (Channel count 2, mask
; 0x3), rotation vector at ~53 Hz reporting -0.41, 0.04, 0.91, 0.04, -1.00 — where the
; final -1.00 is Android's heading-accuracy field meaning UNAVAILABLE.
;
; Verdict 511 when, on Go / Rust / TypeScript / fkwu:
;     1  one sample at 48 kHz is 7 mm of path difference
;     2  one sample at 16 kHz is 21 mm
;     4  across a 160 mm baseline that is a 2506 millidegree bearing step at 48 kHz
;     8  and 7520 millidegrees at 16 kHz — three times coarser for the same geometry
;    16  2.5 degrees at three metres is 131 mm of cross-range: a hand's width
;    32  composed with an attitude that reports -1, the world-frame bearing is -1
;    64  and the chain says so rather than returning the half it knows
;   128  with a calibrated compass at 5 degrees the chain closes at 7506 millidegrees
;   256  and one phone is one station, so the result is a ray and never a point
;
; The teaching: a chain's error is the sum of its links, and a known value composed with an
; unmeasured one is unmeasured. Bit 32 is the honest half of bit 4 — the mic pair really
; does resolve 2.5 degrees, and reporting that as the system's accuracy would be true about
; the component and false about the answer.

(do
    (bearing-chain-check))
